+    
+    Walks the published Quick start as a stranger would, from a throwaway clone at
+    c1896cc. Three arms behave as the README promises (bunker-server-install.sh
+    --check names BUNKER_SERVER; project-node.sh --check reports NODE: FAIL (4) with
+    each missing layer named; node-create.sh names BUNKER_SERVER and stops). The
+    documented clone re-run also reproduces: PASS repo_clone @ df40870 and a
+    separate `git -C "$home/repo" rev-parse HEAD` reads the same sha.
+    
+    The friction is at the end of a SUCCESSFUL create. scripts/node-create.sh:130:
+    
+      [ "$FAILED" -eq 0 ] && { say "NODE CREATED: $AGENT"; say "manifest: /home/<uid>/.node/node.json"; exit 0; }
+    
+    Probe (re-runnable from the repo root):
+    
+      $ grep -n 'manifest: /home/<uid>' scripts/node-create.sh
+      130:[ "$FAILED" -eq 0 ] && { say "NODE CREATED: $AGENT"; say "manifest: /home/<uid>/.node/node.json"; exit 0; }
+      G1_RC=0
+      $ test -e '/home/<uid>/.node/node.json'; echo "named_path_exists=$?"
+      named_path_exists=1
+    
+    The path is a sanitisation artifact, not a value the script substitutes, and it
+    names a node-side file on the control host (specs/NODE.md:5, project-node.sh:297
+    writes "$STATE/node.json"). A user who just succeeded is handed an artifact
+    location that cannot be opened. Filed as CF-179; the repair is future work
+    tracked by that pending row and is NOT expected at this commit.
+    
+    Also recorded, not re-filed: two concurrent node-create runs cross-report each
+    other's spawn error through the fixed /tmp/spawn.log — run B (server bogus-beta)
+    printed `FAIL spawn — bunker: server "bogus-alpha" not found in config`. That is
+    liveness evidence for pending CF-056, whose premise already names the shared
+    path; and node-create.sh:118 still interpolates --project/--repo/--harness
+    unescaped while --ref and CRIER_URL are escaped (CF-159, unchanged).
+    
+    No node host answered this pass (bunker-las-01 refused connections), so the
+    create leg was walked through its documented refusal paths instead; the earlier
+    execution of this tick created and destroyed a node on a reachable host.
+    
+    Guard position, stated honestly: this is a board-only commit, which the repo's
